# An array iterator that a next() finished while another next() of it read the length stays finished: the outer call hands out the element at its own position and stores nothing.
# Where the calls in between only stepped on, the outer call stores its own position behind them, and the next call goes on from there.
# The getter of `length` calls next() on the iterator that is asking. Walked code reads the position again behind the length, and so does the operation that straight code calls.
